ues grew 1.9% to $47.9B in 2025, with flat unit case volume. North America grew 3.8% and EMEA 5.1%. Operating income jumped 37.7% to $13.8B, mainly because 2024 included large fairlife-related charges.","Net income rose 23.3% to $13.1B, or $3.04 per share. A one-time fairlife payment held free cash flow to $5.3B; excluding it, free cash flow was $11.4B. Dividends rose 5.0% to $8.8B."],"highlights":["Operating margin rose 7.5 points to 28.7%.","North America operating income rose 11.3% to $5.1B.","Diluted EPS rose 23.6% to $3.04.","2026 outlook calls for 4%–5% organic revenue growth."],"watch":["Unit case volume was flat.","Free cash flow was cut by the fairlife payment.","Asia Pacific operating income fell 5.3%.","Total debt is $45.5B."],"table":[["Net operating revenues",47.941,47.061,1],["Cost of goods sold",18.397,18.324],["Gross profit",29.544,28.737,1],["Operating expenses",15.782,18.745],["Operating income",13.762,9.992,1],["Equity income & other, net",2.236,3.094],["Income before taxes",15.998,13.086],["Income taxes",2.861,2.437],["Net income to shareowners",13.107,10.631,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",3.04,2.46,0,"eps"],["Operating cash flow",7.408,6.805],["Free cash flow",5.296,4.741,1]],"sources":[["Coca-Cola Q4 and full-year 2025 results (SEC exhibit)","https://investors.coca-colacompany.com/filings-reports/all-sec-filings/content/0001628280-26-006642/a2025q4earningsreleaseex-9.htm"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"North America was 41% of revenue and grew 3.8%.","say":"North America made up 41 percent of revenue, and grew 3.8 percent."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Margins","big":"28.7%","sub":"operating margin · +7.5 pp","lines":["Operating income $13.8B, +37.7%","2024 had fairlife charges"],"cap":"Operating income rose 37.7% to $13.8B, a 28.7% margin.","say":"Operating income rose 37.7 percent to 13.8 billion dollars, a 28.7 percent margin."},{"kicker":"Cash","big":"$11.4B","sub":"free cash flow excluding fairlife payment","lines":["Reported free cash flow $5.3B",